{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Peter Prepares for Final Exams"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Finally Over"}, {"type": "position", "content": 10}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 10}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe characteristics of different people and their jobs"}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn5le10ob10re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The First Conditional"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use the First Conditional to talk about actions and situations in the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "There are two parts to the sentence.  "}, {"type": "text", "content": " One part is the <span class=\"strong\">condition</span>. The other part is the <span class=\"strong\">result</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Form: <br><span class=\"italic\">If + subject + Simple Present tense  + subject + will or can </span><br> You use a comma after the condition in this form.  "}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can change the two parts of the sentence so that the result comes first."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Condition \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Result\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> If I graduate in accounting,  </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'll be able work in many departments. </span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Result \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Condition\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'll take Advanced Accounting Methods next term</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">if I get a good grade this course.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Modals May, Might, Will"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the modals <span class=\"italic\">may</span> and <span class=\"italic\">might</span> to show possibility. They have the same meaning. <br>  You use the modal <span class=\"italic\">will</span> to predict the future in a more certain way."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Modals go before a verb in the base form. The verb does not change."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":1,\"columns\":1,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I think accounting may be a very interesting career.<br> I might do well on the exam.<br> I'll take either Techniques of Leadership or IT Systems next year.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "method "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "way; manner "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'll take the course Advanced Accounting Methods next term."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le10ob10aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about programs of study."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "technique "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "way; manner; method "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  I'll take the course Techniques of Leadership next year."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le10ob10aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "leadership "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the ability to lead and inspire people "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The course Techniques of Leadership is very interesting."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le10ob10aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "IT "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "Information Technology (=computers) "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Maybe I will take the course IT Systems."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le10ob10aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to graduate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to finish studying in a program"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": " Example: When you graduate in accounting, you can work in many departments. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le10ob10aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "advanced"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "at a high level "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Did you take the course Advanced Accounting?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le10ob10aud06"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Think of six actions or events that could take place in your life in the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Decide if each thing is possible or certain."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Talk about each thing. If it is possible, use <span class=\"italic\">may</span> or <span class=\"italic\">might</span>. If it is more certain, use <span class=\"italic\">will</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Ask your partner to talk about actions or events in their future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Discuss the actions or events."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I think of future actions or events."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about future actions or events."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I listen to my partner."}]}], "labs": [{